          "t": 422.0,
          "note": "A yellow stone sits at the left edge of the house, unlabelled in every frame around it, and neither model finds it. The classical detector does find it -- (+1.80,+0.37), confidence 0.86 -- but `to_label` discarded any box crossing the image edge, so every stone within about 0.14 m of the panel boundary was excluded from training. That stone is 1.84 m from the tee: inside the house and counting. The red behind it is a real stone partially occluded by a player, and is correctly labelled.",
